(5695758, 828456, 83313, '<td valign="top">A bit soft and the details are not coming across clearly. I do not see an y compression artifacts, however your file size of only 70k suggests there may be some JPEG compression taking away a bit of clarity here. Compression kills detail. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)</td>', 'A bit soft and the details are not coming across clearly. I do not see an y compression artifacts, however your file size of only 70k suggests there may be some JPEG compression taking away a bit of clarity here. Compression kills detail. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)', '2009-10-21 14:19:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5695760, 828712, 83313, '<td valign="top">Wonderful detail here, and the person strolling through this gives just the right touch.</td>', 'Wonderful detail here, and the person strolling through this gives just the right touch.', '2009-10-21 14:20:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5695766, 828715, 83313, '<td valign="top">Not really grabbing me with this, I''m afraid. Composition comes off to me a little awkward and the reflections are not having any visual impact for me.</td>', 'Not really grabbing me with this, I''m afraid. Composition comes off to me a little awkward and the reflections are not having any visual impact for me.', '2009-10-21 14:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5695776, 828805, 83313, '<td valign="top">At first glance this looks nice, but after the first 2 seconds I see tons of ugly compression artifacts. Your file size of 149k is just under the challenge limit, so I think at some time during working on this, you may have saved it with an excessive amount of compression, or done repeated saves and opens in JPG format. A good workflow is to save your file in an uncompressed format, either TIFF or your image editor''s native format, until you are ready to post the final product. That way you don''t lose any detail.</td>', 'At first glance this looks nice, but after the first 2 seconds I see tons of ugly compression artifacts. Your file size of 149k is just under the challenge limit, so I think at some time during working on this, you may have saved it with an excessive amount of compression, or done repeated saves and opens in JPG format. A good workflow is to save your file in an uncompressed format, either TIFF or your image editor''s native format, until you are ready to post the final product. That way you don''t lose any detail.', '2009-10-21 14:28:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5695788, 828439, 46918, '<td valign="top">Oh wow stunning image...Now I wanna go white water rafting.</td>', 'Oh wow stunning image...Now I wanna go white water rafting.', '2009-10-21 14:35:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5695798, 828434, 83313, '<td valign="top">Sweet car. There are a ton of compression artifacts showing here. You can see them around all the hard edges, especially in the yellow of the roof and around the edges of the trees. (Not to mention the haloing in the sky, a frequent side effect of some treatments) With a file size of only 70k, you had a lot more overhead to use less compression. Compression kills detail. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)</td>', 'Sweet car. There are a ton of compression artifacts showing here. You can see them around all the hard edges, especially in the yellow of the roof and around the edges of the trees. (Not to mention the haloing in the sky, a frequent side effect of some treatments) With a file size of only 70k, you had a lot more overhead to use less compression. Compression kills detail. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (150k for this one)', '2009-10-21 14:38:23.000000', NULL, 1),
